{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "2ed505f4-818f-8b7d-97bc-52e752819100",
  "created_at": "2026-02-25T11:08:40-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Utilities",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Miguel Ortiz",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Tony Ferreira",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T11:06:03-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Utilities billing, this is Tony. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T11:06:07-05:00",
      "duration": 21,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, hello, Tony. This is Miguel Ortiz. I live at 79 Callender Avenue, up the North End, you know. I got a water and sewer bill here and, I mean, I'm a renter. Right? And my landlord says it's mine to pay. But I'm telling you, I never had a bill in my name before. So whose is it? Do you follow me?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T11:06:28-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I follow you, Mr. Ortiz. The water account usually sits in the property owner's name, because the city bills the owner of the property. What the owner and the tenant agree on is between the two of them, so it depends on your lease. Whose name is printed on the bill?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T11:06:45-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Well, it's, um, it's got the landlord's name on top. And mine under it, c/o, I think. Right? That's what it says. So I mean, it's his, no?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T11:06:55-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The account is his, yes. The city will look to him for payment. If your lease says you cover water, he can ask you for it, but that's a lease question, not something I can settle from here."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T11:07:08-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, okay. I mean, nobody told me that when I moved in, you know. Now they send this thing and I'm supposed to just pay it. Anyway. Can you send me another copy? Mine's got coffee on it. By email, if you can."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T11:07:23-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure, I can do that. What email address would you like it sent to? Go slow and spell it for me."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T11:07:31-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh. Um, well, the woman next door, she speaks to me over the hedge every morning, you know, and she does the email for me. Let me get it from her and call you back. Is that all right? Right?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T11:07:45-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's fine. Call back when you have it, and I'll send the copy right then. Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T11:07:51-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah. If I pay it, can I drop it in that box tonight? When you're closed. Does that count as on time, or does it get stamped tomorrow, you know, late?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T11:08:02-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "There's a payment drop box at City Hall. Generally what counts is when it's received, and items in the box are collected the next business morning. If your due date is today, that could be tight, so check the date on the bill. You can also pay online any hour."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T11:08:19-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Online, I don't do that. I mean, I don't have, you know. So the box. And it's due Friday, so tonight is fine, right?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T11:08:27-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Tonight is fine for a Friday due date. Put a check in an envelope with your account number on it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T11:08:34-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Good. Thank you, Tony. Bye now."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T11:08:37-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You're welcome, Mr. Ortiz. Take care."
    }
  ],
